   "id": 511722,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Dave grows wheat (<span data-math=\"w\">w</span>) and barley (<span data-math=\"b\">b</span>) on a farm. Dave expects to profit $150 per acre for wheat and $180 per acre for barley. The objective function for profit in this situation is:",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1000710,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{P = 150w + 180b}\">{P = 150w + 180b}</span>",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000711,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{P = 150b + 180w}\">{P = 150b + 180w}</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000712,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{P = 180w + 150b}\">{P = 180w + 150b}</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000713,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{P = 150w - 180b}\">{P = 150w - 180b}</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response",
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Let <i>w</i> = the number of acres of wheat.</p>\n<p>Let <i>c</i> = the number of acres of barley.</p>\n<p>Let <i>P</i> = the profit.</p>\n<p>The profit on an acre of wheat is $150 and the profit on an acre of barley is $180.</p>\n<p>Break the words into components.</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>The total profit</td>\n<td>is</td>\n<td>$150 times the number of acres of wheat</td>\n<td>plus</td>\n<td>$180 times the number of acres of barley</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><i>P</i></td>\n<td>=</td>\n<td>150<i>w</i></td>\n<td>+</td>\n<td>180<i>b</i></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"P = 150w + 180b\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
